{"seq":16,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/openclaw-opus-full-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T07:16:17.536Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"aca301da49f150f7cd5c4f2490b3c690ee31cc8b460dc9390dfc767394e59754","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"Hi Pree, here are the Marrow Fieldworks ticket numbers I found:\n\n• *#4409*: from Moss's digest \"Central handoffs next week\" (teams/team-central/digests, 2 Jan 2026). It's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, 06:00 flatbed intake). Hollis flagged it before the 5 Jan handoff.\n• *#4412*: same Moss digest. It's a driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots.\n• *PD-5302*: from #central-random, where Hollis posted on 14 Oct (this week) that it's another Marrow Fieldworks ticket for a follow-up from this week. He said no action was needed.\n\nThis one might belong to Fieldworks, but I can't confirm it:\n• *#8841*: from #central-random, where Tobias posted on 13 Oct (this week). It's the West yard Door 2 double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. He tied it to \"Tobias's dealer account\" but didn't name the account. Moss's digest says Fieldworks changed hands on 5 Jan, so it might be Fieldworks, but nothing I can see links the two.\n\nI left these out because they belong to other accounts: FR-882 and PD-4821 (Marrow Agrisupply), and #88412 (Tansleigh Packaging). Moss's Central cheat sheet has no ticket numbers, and there's nothing else in our DM. I don't have access to the Marrow Fieldworks ticket files, so this list only covers notes and chat.","thread_ts":"1792159200.000126"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1792159200.000127","thread_ts":"1792159200.000126"}}
{"seq":17,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/openclaw-opus-full-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T07:16:24.209Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"3474ace43c91569f2a46cb233babe8343f2056850557cbf75ab8e8a9dbba7213","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"I found three Marrow Fieldworks ticket numbers and one more that might be Fieldworks but I can't confirm. I sent Pree the list in our DM, in a thread on her message.\n\n**Marrow Fieldworks tickets:**\n- **#4409**, from Moss's digest \"Central handoffs next week\" (2 Jan 2026): a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard.\n- **#4412**, from the same digest: a driver text-message prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on overflow lots.\n- **PD-5302**, from #central-random (Hollis, 14 Oct): he called it another Marrow Fieldworks ticket, for a follow-up from this week.\n\n**Might be Fieldworks:**\n- **#8841**, from #central-random (Tobias, 13 Oct): West yard Door 2 is double-booking when flatbeds check in early. He linked it to \"Tobias's dealer account\" without naming the account. Moss's digest says Fieldworks changed hands on 5 Jan, but nothing I can see says it went to Tobias, so I flagged it as unconfirmed.\n\n**Left out:**\n- **Other accounts:** FR-882 and PD-4821 are Marrow Agrisupply tickets, and #88412 is Tansleigh Packaging.\n- **Nothing found:** Moss's Central cheat sheet has no ticket numbers, and our DM has nothing beyond her request.\n- **Not covered:** I can't open any Marrow Fieldworks account or ticket files, so the list only covers notes and chat.\n\nI checked that Pree is a member of #central-random and #central-team before reading them. I also didn't use message search, since its results include conversations she can't see. Ticket numbers count as operational facts, so the finance and approval rules didn't apply."},"outcome":"o